XB-Kidux-Name-en: Wikipedia
XB-Kidux-Description-en: Wikipedia, the whole encyclopedia, in the child's language, with the rest of the internet closed. It is written for everyone, not only for children.
XB-Kidux-Name-es: Wikipedia
XB-Kidux-Description-es: Wikipedia, la enciclopedia entera, en el idioma del niño, con el resto de internet cerrado. Está escrita para todo el mundo, no solo para niños.
XB-Kidux-Ages: 8-
Description: Kidux learning module: Wikipedia, a door to the encyclopedia
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. This learning
 module opens Wikipedia in the child's language, in a window of its own,
 with the Wikimedia projects it links to, Wiktionary, Wikibooks and the
 others, and no other website: a link to anywhere else leads nowhere. It
 is the whole of Wikipedia, written for everyone and not only for
 children, so an adult decides whether a child reads it.
 .
 It needs the internet whenever it is used.
 .
 Once it is installed, an adult switches it on for each child on the
 Modules page of the adult panel.
